## Commit 1 — Notification Mongoose model

```
feat(server/F-9): add Notification model — 6 types, Mixed payload, compound index

models/notification.model.ts:

  INotification interface:
    userId:    Types.ObjectId  (ref → User)
    type:      enum 6 values:
                 event_new | deadline | link_received |
                 link_update | credential_update | link_expiring
    payload:   Schema.Types.Mixed  — discriminated per type; stored as-is
    readAt?:   Date              — null = unread; Date = read timestamp
    createdAt: Date              (timestamps: true)

  Indexes:
    { userId: 1, readAt: 1, createdAt: -1 }  — compound (named 'user_notifications')
      Drives GET /notifications (user's unread-first list, cursor-based).
      readAt included so MongoDB can use index for unread-only filter.

  Design decisions:
    Mixed payload — avoids a discriminated union of 6 sub-schemas.
      Trade-off: no Mongo-level schema enforcement per type.
      Acceptable: payload shape is enforced in notification.service (TS types).
    No TTL index — notifications are kept indefinitely (user's history).
      Can add TTL (e.g. 90 days) in F-10 hardening if needed.

Refs: FR-29, FR-30
```

