## Commit 3 — Home feed service

```
feat(server/F-9): home feed service — 30s per-user cache, skill-match fallback, empty-key omission

modules/home/home.service.ts:

  getHomeData(userId):
    Cache key: home:{userId}  TTL: 30s
      Per-user (not global) — each student sees personalised data.
      30s matches the plan spec; short enough for near-real-time feel,
      long enough to absorb repeated tab switches.
      Invalidated explicitly by sendLink(), respondLink(), publishEvent().

    Single Promise.all — 5 parallel queries, no serial waterfalls:
      1. User.findById (name, branch, year, skills, department)
      2. Notification.exists({ userId, readAt: null }) → unreadNotificationsFlag
      3. TeamLink.countDocuments({ toId: userId, status: 'pending' }) → pendingRequestCount
      4. Event.find({ status:'published', deadline: { $lte: now+48h } })
           .sort({ deadline: 1 }).limit(5) → closingSoonEvents
      5a. Skill-match: TeamPost.find({ rolesNeeded: { $in: user.skills }, status:'open' }).limit(5)
      5b. Fallback (no skills): TeamPost.find({ status:'open' }).limit(5)
          (dept/year fallback — ITeamPost has no dept field; fallback is generic open posts)

    Empty-key omission:
      pendingRequestCount=0 → key absent from response (not 0).
      closingSoonEvents=[] → key absent.
      matchedTeamPosts=[]  → key absent.
      Client never renders empty blocks; avoids conditional checks on empty arrays.

    Cache invalidation helpers (exported):
      invalidateHomeCache(userId): invalidateCache('home:' + userId)
      invalidateAllHomeCaches(): invalidateCachePrefix('home:')

Refs: FR-39, FR-40
```

