## Commit 5 — Deadline reminder hourly cron

```
feat(server/F-9): hourly deadline reminder cron — 48h/4h windows, AuditLog dedup, fan-out via members[]

jobs/deadlineReminders.ts:

  scheduleDeadlineReminders():
    node-cron '0 * * * *' — every hour on the hour.
    Two parallel windows per tick (Promise.all):
      48h: events with deadline ∈ [now+47h, now+49h]  → in-app + email
       4h: events with deadline ∈ [now+3h,  now+5h]   → in-app only

    ±1h window (not exact match):
      Handles timing drift from the hourly cron without double-sending.
      AuditLog dedup provides the safety net.

  isAlreadySent(eventId, hoursLeft):
    Checks AuditLog for action='deadline_reminder' with meta.eventId + meta.hoursLeft
    within the last 2 hours.
    Why AuditLog (not an Event field)?
      SRP — separates scheduling concern from domain model.
      AuditLog is already indexed on (action, createdAt).

  Fan-out logic:
    Registration.find({ eventId, status: { $in: ['submitted','locked'] } })
      .select('members')
    Collects unique userIds from members[] where member.status !== 'declined'.
    (IRegistration has no top-level userId — registrants live in members[].userId)
    Team: all non-declined members notified, not just the leader.

  Error handling: try/catch wraps processWindow — never crashes the server process.

Refs: FR-31 (deadline reminders)
```

