## PR Description

```markdown
## F-9: Notifications & Home Feed

### Summary
Email-only notifications (no web push/VAPID). Six notification types written
to MongoDB and optionally emailed for high-value events. Personalised home feed
(30s per-user cache, single round-trip). Hourly deadline reminder cron with
AuditLog dedup. Infinite-scroll notifications page. Unread dot in BottomNav
driven by the already-cached home query — zero extra network requests.

### Changes
- **1 new server model** (`notification.model.ts`)
- **4 new server module files** (`notifications/` — schema, service, controller, routes)
- **3 new server module files** (`home/` — service, controller, routes)
- **1 new server cron job** (`deadlineReminders.ts`)
- **5 modified server files** (`email.service`, `credential.service`, `link.service`, `event.service`, `routes.ts`, `server.ts`)
- **8 new client files** (home: types, API, hook, page · notifications: types, API, hooks, page)
- **2 modified client files** (`router.tsx`, `BottomNav.tsx`)

### Key Design Decisions (SDE3)

| Decision | Rationale |
|----------|-----------|
| Email for 3 types only (`event_new`, `deadline`-48h, `credential_update`) | Conservative — avoids spam. Link events are frequent; 4h reminder too late to act on email |
| Fire-and-forget `sendNotification` | Notification failures must never block or degrade the primary API response |
| AuditLog dedup for cron | Avoids adding `lastRemindedAt` to Event model (SRP). `(action, eventId, hoursLeft)` is a natural dedup key |
| Per-user cache key `home:{userId}` | Global cache would serve wrong user's data after invalidation |
| Empty-key omission in home response | Client never renders empty blocks; avoids all `if (arr.length > 0)` checks |
| Cursor-based pagination | ObjectId cursors are stable under concurrent inserts; `skip()` is not |
| `useHome()` drives BottomNav unread dot | Single source of truth — re-uses 30s warm cache, zero extra requests |
| Fan-out via `Registration.members[]` | `IRegistration` has no top-level `userId`; all non-declined members notified |
| Campus-wide `event_new` fan-out | `IEvent` has no `department` field; eligibility is a feed concern, not notification's |

### Security Checklist
- [x] `/home` reads `userId` from JWT only — never from query params
- [x] `markRead` verifies `notification.userId === req.user.id` before updating
- [x] Notification sending is async — never surfaces errors to API caller
- [x] Deadline cron guarded by AuditLog dedup — no double-sends on drift

### Testing Checklist
- [ ] `GET /home` responds < 500ms on seed data
- [ ] Closing-soon events correct (deadline < now+48h)
- [ ] No-skill student gets generic open-post fallback (not empty)
- [ ] Empty pendingRequestCount/closingSoonEvents/matchedTeamPosts absent from response
- [ ] Verify credential → student notified (in-app + email)
- [ ] Accept/decline link → both parties notified in-app
- [ ] Publish event → all active students receive in-app notification
- [ ] 48h and 4h deadline reminders fire without double-sending (AuditLog checked)
- [ ] `GET /notifications` returns cursor-paginated list
- [ ] `PATCH /notifications/:id/read` is idempotent
- [ ] BottomNav unread dot appears when unreadNotificationsFlag = true

### Refs
FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, FR-39, FR-40
```

